# TFM Scrunch

Public two-page Next.js App Router microsite for a generic Sitecore + Scrunch AEO/GEO audit.
No visitor login. Audits are generated live by Azure OpenAI (org IT AI sandbox; was Gemini);
leads and request events are written
server-side to Firestore.

## Stack

- **Framework**: Next.js (App Router), React 19, Tailwind 4, `next/font/google` (Google Sans)
- **AI**: Azure OpenAI via `ai` + `@ai-sdk/azure`, called only from `src/server/audit/` and
  `src/server/scrunch/` (server-only)
- **Persistence**: Firestore collections `tmf_scrunch_leads`, `tmf_scrunch_reports`,
  `tmf_scrunch_audit_events`, and `tmf_scrunch_settings` (Firebase Admin, server-only) plus a
  local `data/leads.jsonl` fallback — see `src/server/audit/lead-log.ts`. No client Firebase SDK.
  PDFs are stored on the report document (`pdfBase64`). Provider/model live in
  `tmf_scrunch_settings/app`; API keys stay in env.

## Conventions

- All visitor-facing branding/copy constants (company name, presenter, CTA label, event name,
  site URL) live in `src/lib/site-config.ts` — import `SITE` from there, never hardcode strings.
- Server-only AI code stays under `src/server/`, imported only from route handlers or other
  server-only modules — never from a `"use client"` component.
- Client components fetch via plain `fetch()` — there is no auth wrapper (`authFetch`) in this
  project, unlike the parent `SitecoreAiDemoSenario` repo it was forked from.
- Tables/report blocks reuse the same shared visual language as the parent repo's Scrunch
  workspace (rounded cards, `#8629ff` accent, `#17141f` dark panels) for a consistent brand feel.

## Docs

- README.md — overview, how to run locally, how the audit works
- AGENTS.md — paths and conventions for AI coding agents

## Deploy

Vercel (or similar): set provider keys (`AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY`, `AZURE_OPENAI_RESOURCE_NAME`,
and/or `GEMINI_API_KEY`) plus `FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON` and
`NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID` (required to persist leads and settings), `LEADS_ADMIN_SECRET`
(stand desk), `AZURE_OPENAI_API_VERSION` (optional), `NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL` (optional,
defaults to sitecore.com). Switch Azure vs Gemini and the model from `/stand-desk/settings`
(`AI_PROVIDER` / `AZURE_OPENAI_DEPLOYMENT` / `GEMINI_MODEL` are fallbacks). Bot protection is
Vercel BotID (no extra keys). Email sending is disabled.
